# Docker build context excludes — added 2026-09-01.
#
# Why this file exists: render.yaml builds with `runtime: docker` and the
# Dockerfile ends in `COPY . .`, so WITHOUT this file the entire build context
# is baked into the production image. Two consequences, one of them a security
# problem:
#
#   1. Size. Locally the context is ~1.7 GB of things the image never needs
#      (node_modules 815M, frontend/.next 587M, venv 179M, .git 157M).
#   2. Secrets. `.env` and `.secrets/` are gitignored, so they are absent from
#      Render's clone — but a `docker build .` run on this machine WOULD copy
#      real credentials into an image layer. Excluding them here makes that
#      impossible regardless of who builds.
#
# ⚠️ What is deliberately NOT excluded, and why — do not "optimise" these away:
#   docs/ frontend/ tests/ scripts/  are read AT RUNTIME by the in-process
#   APScheduler cron jobs (services/scheduler/cron_jobs.py). The legal scans
#   read frontend/ sources for forbidden terms, marketing_daily_dispatch reads
#   docs/marketing/{content-bank.json,week1-cards/*.png}, and ship_blockers
#   reads SHIP_BLOCKERS.md. Dropping them would silently break those jobs.

# ── Version control ──
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.github

# ── Local virtualenvs / dependency trees (reinstalled from requirements.txt) ──
venv
.venv
**/node_modules

# ── Frontend build output — Vercel serves the frontend, not this image ──
frontend/.next
frontend/out
frontend/.vercel

# ── Secrets & local env (see note above — this is the security-relevant part) ──
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.secrets
*.pem
*.key

# ── Local databases & instance state ──
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
instance
.kis_token_cache.json

# ── Caches & build junk ──
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.DS_Store

# ── Local-only run artifacts (regenerated; never read by the web service) ──
qa
reports
state
legal_monitor_artifacts
self_healing_artifacts
.bug-hunt
.bughunt-*
BUG_SWEEP_*.md

# ── Editor / tooling ──
.obsidian
.vercel
.bkit

# ── research-desk (독립 Next.js 프로젝트, 2026-09-17) — 백엔드 이미지와 무관 ──
research-desk
